    "question": {
      ":question/id": "67a16f1f-b4da-5d67-85e2-5c36fbfd360b",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{x - 3}}{\\sqrt{y - 6}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{x - 3}}{\\sqrt{y - 6}} \\\\ (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\sqrt{x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y - 6})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 \\sqrt{x - 3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2 \\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} & =\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+K \\\\ \\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}} & =2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3}{2}K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\left(y - 6\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
