    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0edc7e53-b5b2-5ed8-858c-68965210f97f",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(4 x + 20\\right) e^{2 - y}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(4 x + 20\\right) e^{2 - y} \\\\ (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 x + 20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y - 2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4 x + 20)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ e^{y - 2} & =2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y - 2}=2 \\left(x + 5\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
