      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\left(12 - 4 x\\right) e^{- y - 4} \\\\ (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 - 4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (e^{y + 4})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (12 - 4 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ e^{y + 4} & =- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y + 4}=- 2 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}+C.\n$$",
